{"id":"fort-vaux","name":"Fort Vaux","qid":"Q1438801","country":"France","locality":"Douaumont-Vaux, Vaux-devant-Damloup","lat":"49.19993889","lon":"5.469975","built":"1881","year":1881,"year_text":"1881","century":"19th century","era":"19th century","period":"","date_basis":"description text (approximate)","style":"","heritage":"classified historical monument","type":"fort","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Vaux","text":"Fort Vaux (French: Fort de Vaux), in Vaux-Devant-Damloup, Meuse, France, was a polygonal fort forming part of the ring of 19 large defensive works intended to protect the city of Verdun. Built from 1881 to 1884 for 1,500,000 francs, it housed a garrison of 150 men. Vaux was the second fort to fall in the Battle of Verdun after Fort Douaumont, which was captured by a small German raiding party in February 1916 in the confusion of the French retreat from the Woëvre plain.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Vaux","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-4988468b05ab","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"Fort de Vaux - extérieur.JPG","o":"gh-4988468b05ab.jpg","credit":{"text":"historicair 01:45, 15 October 2006 (UTC)","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_de_Vaux_-_ext%C3%A9rieur.JPG","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"battlefield-1--fort-de-vaux","game":"battlefield-1","name":"Fort De Vaux","verified":false,"text":"Fort De Vaux Fort De Vaux is a map featured in the Battlefield 1: They Shall Not Pass expansion. It takes place during the Battle of Verdun in the German raid of Fort de Vaux in 1916.","text_source":"https://battlefield.fandom.com/wiki/Fort_De_Vaux","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-132b2f5a564a","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-132b2f5a564a.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Battlefield 1, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://battlefield.fandom.com/wiki/File:Fort_De_Vaux_09.jpg","vi